PNEC versioned additive baseline: 0001_pnec_release (28 release tables).

PROPOSED FOR MAINTAINER/OPERATOR REVIEW. Run only on disposable databases until
schema inspection, backup/restore rehearsal and operator approval are complete.
Production worker startup performs no initialization; development retains its
existing create_all/legacy compatibility behavior.

The frozen baseline preflights existing release tables before DDL. It creates
missing release tables and adds only four recognized nullable legacy users
columns (bio, avatar_url, phone, auth_token), including the new token index.
Unexpected columns/types/nullability/constraints require a separate reviewed
migration. Extra tables/columns are preserved, not removed. Do not blindly stamp.

Run once, with worker traffic stopped and correct operator-managed environment:
  python -m flask --app main db upgrade
  python -m flask --app main release-seed --approved

Never use db_init.py, drop_all, db downgrade, or an older environment by accident.
A downgrade deliberately refuses to drop tables or columns. Roll back the app
image against the additive schema after compatibility checks. Restoring a backup
is a separately approved data-recovery operation with potential loss of later
writes. MySQL and SQLite DDL are not assumed transactional; inspect partial
failures and rehearse on a sanitized clone. See deploy/RELEASE_RUNBOOK.md and
DATABASE_RECOVERY.md for prerequisites and operator gates.
